KEY INSIGHTS

Malaria incidence increased significantly during periods of higher temperature in Niger State (r = 0.775).

Humidity showed moderate positive correlation with malaria cases in Kaduna (r = 0.551) and FCT (r = 0.461), indicating increased transmission risk in humid conditions.

Some states showed weak or negative correlations, suggesting additional contributing factors such as sanitation, healthcare access, and mosquito control interventions.

